{title: O Master, Let Me Walk with Thee}
{artist: Washington Gladden / H. Percy Smith}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Closing}
{key: D}
{key_original: Eb}
{tempo: 100}
{time: 3/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (The Psalter (Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania: United Presbyterian Board of Publication, 1912), # 241)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]O Master, [G]let__[D]__ me [Em]walk with [A]Thee,
[A]In [Bm]low[A7]ly [D]paths [Bm]of [E7]service [A7]free;
[A7]Tell me Thy [D]secret; [G]help me [Em]bear
[D]The [A7]strain [Bm]of [A7]toil, [D]the [Em]fret [A]of [D]care.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Help me the [G]slow__[D]__ of [Em]heart to [A]move
[A]By [Bm]some [A7]clear, [D]win[Bm]ning [E7]word of [A7]love;
[A7]Teach me the [D]wayward [G]feet to [Em]stay,
[D]And [A7]guide [Bm]them [A7]in [D]the [Em]home[A]ward [D]way.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]O Master, [G]let__[D]__ me [Em]walk with [A]Thee,
[A]Be[Bm]fore [A7]the [D]taunt[Bm]ing [E7]Phari[A7]see;
[A7]Help me to [D]bear the [G]sting of [Em]spite,
[D]The [A7]hate [Bm]of [A7]men [D]who [Em]hide [A]Thy [D]light.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]The sore dis[G]trust__[D]__ of [Em]souls sin[A]cere
[A]Who [Bm]can[A7]not [D]read [Bm]Thy [E7]judgments [A7]clear,
[A7]The dullness [D]of the [G]multi[Em]tude,
[D]Who [A7]dim[Bm]ly [A7]guess [D]that [Em]Thou [A]art [D]good.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[D]Teach me Thy [G]pa__[D]__tience; [Em]still with [A]Thee
[A]In [Bm]clos[A7]er, [D]dear[Bm]er, [E7]compa[A7]ny,
[A7]In work that [D]keeps faith [G]sweet and [Em]strong,
[D]In [A7]trust [Bm]that [A7]tri[D]umphs [Em]ov[A]er [D]wrong.
{end_of_verse}
